// 2026-11-18 (issue #7, Phase 2): outlined-guard exercise.
//
// The canonical outlinable shape (see term_valid_swan_song.bv) is a guard
// whose body is a single observable expression over PURE scalar reads:
// `endprogram Print#(a)`. Such a body is outlined into
// `@txn_<name>_cold_N` by the cold-function outlining pass — the FFI call
// becomes a memory barrier, and the body is rewritten so every state
// identifier is read through a `__cp_<name>` param instead of `%state`.
//
// This fixture exercises the expression shapes `rewrite_expr_idents`
// handles inside an outlined body:
//   * Identifier reads (a, b)
//   * BinaryOp over identifiers (a * b)
//   * a call whose arg is a binary op (Print#(a * b))
//   * an `endprogram` with a value arg (the observable that triggers the
//     cold barrier)
//
// The post-outline validation (`validate_cold_body_idents`) confirms no
// identifier survives the rewrite unresolved (a silent-zero gap would fire a
// loud diagnostic here). Expected: builds with NO validation warning and
// prints `a*b` once, then exits.
let a: Int = 3;
let b: Int = 4;

node n [a < 10][a >= 10] {
  a = a + 1;
  when a >= 10 { endprogram Print#(a * b); };
};
